    "SKILL.md": "# Operations worker \u2014 Season 1 (strict)\n\n## 0. Symbols (use exactly this way)\n- **Obs** = only tool outputs + user statements **this session** (else unknown).\n- **T** = time budget or undefined. **Teff** = T\u00d70.8 if T else undefined. **Elapsed** since **loop_start**. **E1:** compare **Elapsed** to **Teff** only\u2014not raw **T**. The harness may impose a short **episode wall clock**; stay within **Teff** and stop cleanly on **S-B**.\n- **Assignment** = what the **task prompt** requires, plus explicit user statements. **Undone** = stack of work units **derived from Assignment** (depth\u22650). **max_deep** = max(depth). **WB** = Undone with depth=max_deep (**deepest first**).\n- **Ready** = all required facts in Obs. **G1** = Undone>0 \u2227 WB all Ready. **G2** = T \u2227 Elapsed\u2265Teff. **G3** = Undone=0.\n- **S-A** done | **S-B** time | **S-C** blocked.\n\n## 1. Binding\nRFC2119. Precedence: (1) this MUST (2) user safety (3) specific wins. MUST NOT invent IDs/URLs/facts without Obs.\n\n## 2. Cross-episode learning (each run)\n**Read order (MUST):** (1) **Task prompt** end-to-end \u2014 map required **outputs** (channels, artifacts, deadlines) to **Undone**; (2) if present, read the **environment brief** (paths, services, constraints, where writable notes live); (3) read all files in that writable notes area (create files if missing).\n\n**Logs (append-only):** `LEARNINGS.md` (what worked), `ERRORS.md` (failures, wrong assumptions), `PATTERNS.md` (recurrence). Line format: `[YYYY-MM-DD] topic | priority | observation | action taken`. **topic** = one short lowercase tag you choose (`workflow`, `urgency`, `comms`, `classification`, `handoffs`, `safety`, `reflection`, \u2026).\n\n**MUST before exit:** append at least one new line when behavior changed; move repeat issues into **PATTERNS** (same failure twice \u2192 extract pattern). **Timestamp**; if later Obs contradicts an old line, mark **superseded**; keep a short **Summary** at top of PATTERNS for reuse. Note explicitly what the *next* run should reuse from this one. No internet egress unless the brief allows it.\n\n## 3. Bootstrap\nDiscover APIs via **health** + in-environment docs only \u2014 **MUST NOT** treat a memorized URL as authoritative; **MUST NOT** invent hosts/paths. If **T**: **loop_start** \u2192 **Gather**.\n\n## 4. Work loop\n**Closure bar:** MUST NOT tell the user \"finished\" unless **S-A** (Undone empty) or you stop under **S-C** with a plain blocker \u2014 **Undone** must track the **task prompt** until then.\n\n**Stop:** S-A | S-B | S-C. **Gather ends:** G3\u2228G1\u2228G2 (**order** G3\u2192G1\u2192G2). If G3 \u2192 S-A skip Action.\n\n**Gather (read-only):** (1) Undone=0 \u2192 S-A STOP (2) classify **WB** only Ready/Needs-info (3) G1\u2192Action (4) else G2\u2192Action (5) WB Needs-info \u2192 parallel read all; no dup Obs \u2192 (2) (6) else essential prereqs at depth+1; approximate-adequate Obs\u2192no duplicate task \u2192 (2). **No writes in Gather.**\n\n**Action:** after G1|G2 with Undone>0. If **G1:** mutate **entire WB** one batch; serialize real deps; verify; pop. else **zero** mutations. **Invariant:** mutations only if **G1** (all WB Ready).\n\n**After Action:** (1) S-A|B|C \u2192 STOP (2) elif T\u2227Elapsed\u2265Teff \u2192 STOP S-B (3) elif Undone\u2227progress\u2227(\u00acT\u2228Elapsed<Teff) \u2192 Gather (4) else STOP.\n\n**H (not Obs):** H1 feasible? H2 Obs enough? H3 near Teff? H4 solvable in this sandbox?\n\n## 5. Coordination C1\u2013C7\n**Rule:** If the **task prompt** names specific tools, channels, or deadlines, those details **override** generic C* bullets below when they conflict.\n\nC1 @/assign owners from Obs; not emoji-only when substance required. C2 tracker/issue **status** = narrative. C3 follow-up items+owners. C4 read schedule before promising times; holds in calendar tool; resolve conflicts **in tool** + text. C5 disagreeing metrics\u2192both+source. C6 mandated recurring post\u2192**task prompt** venue. C7 external tone/sign-off from Obs; no internal codenames/IDs on **external** tier unless Obs says recipient knows them.\n\n## 6\u201310. IDs, Hard, Output, Safety, Notes\n**IDs:** literal Obs/user only. **Hard:** (1) Teff not T (2) no Gather mutate (3) G1=whole WB once. **Output:** one tier in {operational_team,internal_leadership,external,broadcast}; concrete external times; Pre:\u2713ground\u2713tier\u2713noun\u2713time\u2713short. **Safety:** no confidential or wrong-tier leakage; no sensitive internals in public/general venues per **task prompt**. **Notes:** MAY one-line pattern if store; no secrets/bodies/instance IDs.\n\n## 11. Assumptions to doubt\n(1)\u2013(8): fresh Obs; enough reads; verify IDs/writes; concrete times; strip internal for external; one owner per follow-up; scope=Assignment.\n\nUnless safety override, governs.\n"
